---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../data/services';
const service = serviceBySlug('national-diabetes-services-scheme')!;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the NDSS?', a: 'The National Diabetes Services Scheme is an Australian Government initiative, administered by Diabetes Australia, that helps people with diabetes access subsidised products and support. Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair is an NDSS access point, so registered people can collect supplies from us.' },
  { q: 'How do I register for the NDSS?', a: 'Registration needs a form signed by your doctor or a credentialled diabetes educator. The GPs at Help Medical, an independent general practice located inside our store, can help you with this.' },
  { q: 'What do I need to bring to collect NDSS supplies?', a: 'Just show your NDSS card or number at the counter. No appointment is needed; come in any day we’re open.' },
  { q: 'What NDSS supplies can I collect at Pacific Fair?', a: 'Blood glucose test strips, urine and blood ketone test strips, pen needles and syringes, pump consumables, and continuous and flash glucose monitoring products for eligible people. Call us if you’d like to check we have your product in stock.' },
  { q: 'Do you stock supplies for my meter?', a: 'We stock products for all the major meter and monitoring brands. If your product isn’t on the shelf, ask us and we’ll order it in.' },
  { q: 'Do you have blood glucose meters and FreeStyle Libre sensors in stock?', a: `Usually, yes. Sensors and some test strips can sell out, so call us on ${site.phone} to check before you come in. If we’ve sold out, we can usually order it in for the next day.` },
  { q: 'Can I get my diabetes medicines through the NDSS?', a: 'No. The NDSS covers supplies such as test strips and needles. Medicines for diabetes are prescription medicines, so bring us your prescription or send your eScript ahead as usual.' },
  { q: 'Can I check my risk of type 2 diabetes?', a: 'Yes. Do a free AUSDRISK questionnaire at the Health Station inside our store any day we’re open, with a pharmacist nearby to talk through the result.' },
];
---

<ServicePage
  service={service}
  title="Glucose Monitors & Test Strips | Priceline Pacific Fair"
  description="Blood glucose monitors, test strips, FreeStyle Libre sensors and pen needles at Priceline Pacific Fair, Broadbeach. Collect NDSS supplies with no appointment."
  h1="Glucose monitors, test strips and NDSS supplies at Pacific Fair"
  lead="Yes, Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair in Broadbeach usually has blood glucose monitors, test strips and FreeStyle Libre sensors in stock, and we’re an NDSS access point. If you’re registered with the National Diabetes Services Scheme, you can collect subsidised test strips, pen needles, pump consumables and glucose monitoring products from us. Just show your NDSS card or number at the counter; no appointment is needed. Our pharmacists can also help with setting up a new monitor, storing your medicines and sick-day advice."
  faqs={faqs}
  primaryCta={{ label: `Call ${site.phone}`, href: site.phoneHref, event: 'cta_call' }}
  secondaryCta={{ label: 'Hours & directions', href: '/visit-us/' }}
  dateModified="2026-10-29"
>
  <h2>What is the NDSS?</h2>
  <p>The NDSS is an Australian Government initiative, administered by Diabetes Australia, that helps people with diabetes access subsidised products and support. You can learn more at <a href="https://www.ndss.com.au/" rel="noopener">ndss.com.au</a>.</p>

  <h2>How do I register for the NDSS?</h2>
  <p>Registration needs a form signed by your doctor or credentialled diabetes educator. The GPs at <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a>, an independent general practice located inside our store, can help. Once you’re registered, just show your NDSS card or number when you collect supplies.</p>

  <h2>Which NDSS supplies can I collect at Pacific Fair?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>blood glucose test strips</li>
    <li>urine and blood ketone test strips</li>
    <li>pen needles and syringes</li>
    <li>pump consumables</li>
    <li>continuous and flash glucose monitoring products, for eligible people</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We stock products for all the major meter and monitoring brands, including Accu-Chek, FreeStyle, Contour and CareSens. If we don’t have your product on the shelf, we can order it in.</p>
  <p>Medicines for diabetes are prescription medicines and aren’t supplied through the NDSS. See <a href="/prescriptions/">prescriptions</a> for how to send your script ahead.</p>

  <h2>Do you have blood glucose monitors, test strips and Libre sensors in stock?</h2>
  <p>Yes. We usually keep blood glucose monitors (meters), test strips, lancets and FreeStyle Libre sensors in stock at Pacific Fair. Sensors and some test strips can sell out, so call us on <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> to check before you come in. If we’ve sold out, we can usually order it in for the next day.</p>

  <h2>How can our pharmacists support you?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>setting up and using a new meter</li>
    <li>storing your diabetes medicines safely, including in Gold Coast summer heat</li>
    <li>sick-day advice and what to do if your levels are out of range</li>
    <li>checking interactions with other medicines</li>
    <li>disposing of sharps properly</li>
  </ul>
  <p>There’s no appointment needed. Ask at the counter, or call us on <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> if you’d like to check we have your product in stock before you visit.</p>

  <h2>Not diagnosed but worried about type 2 diabetes?</h2>
  <p>Try a free AUSDRISK risk check at our <a href="/health-station/">Health Station</a>. It’s a short questionnaire that estimates your risk of developing type 2 diabetes in the next five years, and our pharmacists can talk you through the result.</p>
</ServicePage>
